    "final_answer": "From MDN’s `container-type` CSS property page at https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/container-type:\n\nFormal definition (required rows)\n- Initial value: normal  \n  - Source: “Formal definition” section, rowheader “Initial value” with cell “normal”.\n- Applies to: all elements  \n  - Source: “Formal definition” section, rowheader “Applies to” with cell “all elements”.\n\nFormal syntax keyword values shown on this page\nThe dedicated “Formal syntax” block only shows structural operators (`[`, `]`, `|`, `||`), but the allowed value keywords for `container-type` are explicitly listed in the “Values” section and are also reflected as subfeature names in the compatibility table. The keyword values visible on this page for the property’s value space are:\n- normal  \n- size  \n- inline-size  \n- scroll-state  \n- anchored\n\n(There is no single printed BNF-like line that lists these together in the visible “Formal syntax” section; the keywords themselves are derived from the clearly labeled “Values” entries and the matching compatibility subfeature row headers.)\n\nDesktop browser compatibility for the base `container-type` property\nFrom the “Browser compatibility” table, in the row whose rowheader is exactly `container-type` and looking only at the desktop columns for the base property (not the individual keyword rows):\n- Chrome (desktop): Full support 105  \n  - Source cell text: “Chrome – Full support 105”\n- Firefox (desktop): Full support 110  \n  - Source cell text: “Firefox – Full support 110”\n- Safari (desktop): Full support 16  \n  - Source cell text: “Safari – Full support 16”\n\nUnavailable / not shown\n- Any additional qualifiers on the initial value beyond the literal keyword `normal`: unavailable.  \n- Any additional constraints on “Applies to” beyond “all elements”: unavailable.  \n- A single, fully written formal-syntax code line containing all the keywords together: unavailable in the visible DOM; only structural operators and the spec link are shown.\n\nThis satisfies the stopping condition: the formal definition’s key rows, the value keywords shown for the property, and the three requested desktop-browser compatibility entries for the base `container-type` property have been recorded.",
